Extra Data:
-----------

SUID (Set User ID) - 4 in first digit  → -perm -4000
SGID (Set Group ID) - 2 in first digit → -perm -2000
Sticky Bit - 1 in first digit  -perm -1000

Remember:
-perm 4000 = Exactly 4000 (no other bits)
-perm -4000 = All these bits must be set (SUID + anything else)
-perm /4000 = Any of these bits set (SUID OR SGID OR Sticky)

Notation	   Equivalent octal	What it finds
-perm -u=s	   -perm -4000	-> Files with SUID set
-perm -g=s	   -perm -2000	 -> Files with SGID set
-perm -o=t	   -perm -1000	 -> Files with sticky bit set
                                          

Find and compress all log files older than 7 days
find /tmp -type f -size -2M -name "*.conf" -exec tar -czvf uploaded.tar.gz {} +

find /etc -type f -size -2M -name "*.conf" -exec cp {} /tmp/ \; 2>/dev/null | wc -l

find / -type f -perm /002 2>/dev/null |wc -l  -> find fies everyone with writable
find / -type f -perm /o=w 2>/dev/null |wc -l  ->  find fies everyone with writable

find / -type f -perm /4002 2>/dev/null |wc -l  -> find fies everyone with writable and set user id

find / -type f -user rohal 2>/dev/null |wc -l  -> user with username
find / -type f -user 1000 2>/dev/null |wc -l  -> user with userID

 Find files where user doesn't have read permission
find /home/jdoe -type f -user rohal ! -perm -u=r

find /home/jdoe -type f ! -perm -u=r	Files owner cannot read
find /home/jdoe -type f ! -perm -g=r	Files group cannot read
find /home/jdoe -type f ! -perm -o=r	Files others cannot read
find /home/jdoe -type f ! -perm /444	Files no one has read permission (user, group, others)


Find executable files owned by root in /usr/local/bin
find /usr/local/bin -type f -user root -perm -u=x
